    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.61) stands as our premier play. His high efficiency score is driven by a favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano; the combination of a high-leverage #3 spot in the order and a targetable opponent SP_xERA of 4.80 makes him an elite start, assuming he cements that top-order slot. Close behind are **Luis Arraez** (63.80) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.75), both benefiting from favorable conditions in the Martin (R) matchup. While the wind blowing out adds a positive multiplier to their upside, **Jung Hoo Lee** remains a critical component of our strategy given the focus on stolen base scarcity, even with a slight drag from the opponent's 60% base-stealing hold rate. **Taylor Ward** also warrants attention; despite a dynamic platoon penalty, his park factor (+16%) and top-of-the-order usage keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" category at 61.76.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.07). While his talent level is unimpeachable, he faces a tough southpaw in C. S\u00e1nchez with an elite SP_xERA of 2.86. The combination of wind blowing in and a negative SP skill adjustment pushes him to the bottom of our active recommendations. **Gavin Sheets** (51.91) is our most marginal start, narrowly edging out **Drew Gilbert** (47.19) for the final utility spot. **Drew Gilbert** fell just short of the lineup because his projected #9 spot triggers a significant order penalty, negating the positive impact of the wind and his potential as a speed asset. As we manage our game caps, we will continue to monitor **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Lawrence Butler**, who remain sidelined due to injury or non-active status, leaving us to rely on the depth provided by **Jonathan Aranda**, **Bryson Stott**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Matt Chapman** to carry the load across the 5x5 categories.",
